  "chunk": "tions about the nature and extent of their reasoning capabilities.\n1 Introduction\nRecent advances in Large Language Models (LLMs) have demonstrated impres-\nsive performance across a wide range of tasks, from code generation to idea\ngeneration, and from assistance in engineering problems to sparking creativity.\nThese impressive capabilities have renewed optimistic predictions about the im-\nminent arrival of Artificial General Intelligence (AGI) or human-level AI [5].\n1\narXiv:2602.15867v1  [cs.CL]  27 Jan 2026\nHowever, such predictions echo earlier waves of AI optimism that ultimately\nfailed to materialize. As Mitchell [24] observes, the field of AI has cycled sev-\neral times between periods of optimistic predictions and substantial investments\n(“AI spring”) and periods of disappointment, loss of confidence, and reduced\nfunding (“AI winter”). From Herbert Simon’s 1960 declaration that “machines\nwill be capable, within twenty years, of doing any work that a man can do”",
